    "lawCode": "Amd §§142 & 143, Ec Dev L",
    "lawSection": "Economic Development Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4888\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the economic development law, in\nrelation to the publication of information regarding awards of state\ncontracts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to publish and announce agencies that have\nentered into a contract\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 would authorize the commissioner to publish and announce that\nan agency has entered into a contract in the procurement opportunities\nnewsletter.\n\nSection 2 would authorize an agency that enters into a contract shall\nsubmit an announcement of the intended contract for inclusion in the\nprocurement opportunities newsletter.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, there is no mechanism in place once the initial contract is\nannounced to know when an agency has entered into a contract. By placing\nthe announcement in the procurement newsletter it would allow MWBEs to\nknow who to contact in order to bid as sub-contractors.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: S2842 - REFERRED TO COMMERCE, ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT AND SMALL\nBUSINESS\n2015-16: S.7304 - Referred to Commerce, Economic Development and Small\nBusiness\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law; provided, however, that effective immediately, the commis-\nsioner of economic development, or his or her delegate, shall promulgate\nrules and regulations and take all other necessary actions to implement\nthe provisions of this act on or before such effective date.\n",
